x86_64-windows  a destructible local (a std::string, and the ledger's watcher) and a `try` in one function is refused for this target: a Microsoft cleanup is a funclet and a state in the FH3 tables rather than a row in a call-site list, and the splitting the Itanium path learned has no counterpart there yet. `catch (std::bad_alloc &)` itself is no longer refused here - the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain reached classes on 2026-09-26 - and the half that needs no exception, `new (std::nothrow)` and the new handler, is new-nothrow.cpp and runs on this target.
tms6747  the emulator's runtime has no `std::set_new_handler`, no nothrow `operator new` and no `std::bad_alloc` - `<new>` declares them as TI's rts6740 exports them, and the emulator answers "undefined symbol" at the first. A program that uses none of them, placement-array-new.cpp, runs here.
